Section 190 of the Cr.P.C provides as under:-
"190. Cognizance of offences by Magistrates- PRAVEEN (1) Subject to the provisions of this Chapter, any KUMAR Magistrate of the first class, and any Magistrate of the Digitally signed by second class specially empowered in this behalf under PRAVEEN KUMAR Date: 2023.04.21 15:24:12 +0530 sub-section (2), may take cognizance of any offence- (a) upon receiving a complaint of facts which constitute such offence;
(b) upon a police report of such facts;
(c) upon information received from any person other than a police officer, or upon his own knowledge, that such offence has been committed.
